---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/quote/QuoteForm.tsx';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/schema/service';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema/faqPage';
import { getAllProducts } from '../../data/catalog/shopify';
import '../../styles/quote-form.css';

const allProducts = await getAllProducts();
const products = allProducts.filter((p) => p.tags.includes('arch')).slice(0, 9);

const faqs = (await getCollection('faq'))
  .filter((f) => f.data.pages.includes('arches'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((f) => ({ question: f.data.question, body: f.body.trim() }));

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Balloon arches',
    description:
      'Custom organic, hoop, and geometric balloon arches built and installed for events in London Ontario.',
    startingPrice: 299,
    url: '/services/balloon-arches',
  }),
];
if (faqs.length > 0) {
  schemas.push(faqPageSchema(faqs.map((f) => ({ question: f.question, answer: f.body }))));
}
---

<BaseLayout
  topic="Balloon Arches"
  description="Custom balloon arches in London Ontario. Organic, hoop, and geometric, built to your colours and venue and installed by us. Most arches land between $499 and $999."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services' },
    { name: 'Balloon arches', url: '/services/balloon-arches' },
  ]}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Install type"
    headline="Balloon arches in London, Ontario"
    subhead="Organic, hoop, and geometric. Built to your venue's measurements and colour palette, then delivered and installed by us."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/quote', label: 'Start a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/portfolio', label: 'See arch work' }}
    image="/images/categories/arches-garlands.webp"
    imageAlt="Custom balloon arch framing a venue entrance"
    variant="page"
  />

  <section class="install-body section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        The arch is the photo most events end up remembering. It marks the entrance, frames the
        ceremony, or anchors the corner everyone gravitates to, and it is doing that job in the
        background of every photo taken near it for the rest of the night.
      </p>

      <h2>What a balloon arch costs in London</h2>
      <p>
        Small organic arches for a photo spot, a classroom, or a home party start around $299. Standard
        doorway and ceremony arches land between $499 and $999. Large statement arches for ballrooms,
        grand openings, and full ceremony backdrops run past $1,200 once they need a structure built
        underneath to hold the shape.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three things move that number. Height and span are the obvious ones, since a fourteen-foot
        ballroom entrance is a different build from a six-foot doorway rather than a bigger version of
        it. Colour count matters more than people expect, because every added colour is a separate
        inflation batch and a separate sort before Brenda starts. And the venue decides the method,
        since what you can attach to, and whether anything can be attached at all, changes how the arch
        has to be supported.
      </p>

      <h2>Organic, hoop, and geometric</h2>
      <p>
        Organic arches are the asymmetric style with clustered balloons in varying sizes, heavier at one
        end and trailing off at the other. It is the most requested look and the most forgiving in a
        room that is not perfectly square. Hoop arches use a visible circular frame with balloons
        arranged around part of it, which reads more structured and photographs well straight on.
        Geometric arches use square or angular framing for a sharper, more modern look, and they suit
        brand activations where the shape should feel deliberate. Full arches cross overhead. Half
        arches climb one side and stop, which costs less and often suits a doorway better because
        nobody has to walk under it.
      </p>

      <h2>About "balloon arch rental"</h2>
      <p>
        People search for a rental, so it is worth being direct about what we do. Nothing here is rented
        or reused. Every arch is built fresh for your date from new materials in your palette, installed
        on site, and taken down afterward if you want that handled. Pricing reflects the build rather
        than a rental period, which is why a quote depends on your specifics rather than a daily rate.
        More on that in the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Related install types</h2>
      <p>
        Looking for something that runs along a wall, a staircase, or a head table instead? That is a
        <a href="/services/balloon-garlands">balloon garland</a>, and it prices differently. If you want
        a solid photo background rather than a frame to stand under, see
        <a href="/services/walls-backdrops">walls and backdrops</a>. Many setups pair an arch at the
        entrance with a wall at the photo corner, and booking them together saves a second setup trip.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {products.length > 0 && (
    <section class="install-products section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shop the catalog</p>
          <h2>Balloon arches in the catalog</h2>
          <p class="lede">Pick a build as-is or use one as the starting point for a custom version.</p>
        </header>
        <ProductGrid products={products} columns={3} />
        <p class="section-link-wrap">
          <a class="section-link" href="https://shop.balloonia.events/collections/arches-garlands">View all arches →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {faqs.length > 0 && <FAQAccordion heading="Balloon arch questions" faqs={faqs} />}

  <section class="install-quote section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Custom build</p>
        <h2>Need something specific?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Send your venue, colours, and a reference photo. Brenda quotes within 24 hours.</p>
      </header>
      <QuoteForm client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--line-relaxed);
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .section-head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .install-quote {
    background: var(--color-paper-soft);
  }
  .section-link {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .section-link-wrap {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }
</style>
